Notes — your persistent memory, in `/n`:
- Earlier sessions, the operator and you wrote these down because the obvious guess was wrong or unknown. A note OVERRIDES your assumptions.
- Before you act on any fact about the environment — which host, where code lives, how to build, deploy, update, configure or reach something, what the user prefers — find the notes below that cover it and read them. Do this also when you feel sure: that feeling is how notes get skipped.
- Ask the user only what the notes do not answer. When you learn such a fact, write or update a note.

